    (h.req "01a1b49c-ac2b-753a-83fc-237e3776c6e1"
      "The judge refuses a transcript that drops, duplicates, reorders or invents a scenario, fragment, reassembly or refusal, reports a line of a recognised kind that is incomplete or has extra fields, or any record that is not a links line, reports a refusal with the wrong class or none, or reports a fragment, reassembly or boundary that differs from the host reference. The host reference refuses a gap, a reordering, a run that never ends, a final fragment followed by another, an unreliable fragment, a fragment with extensions, a fragment that is another message, a fragment with no data, a message whose payload length is wrong, a batch too small for a fragment, and a sequence number that is noncanonical, over 32 bits, six bytes or truncated, with a noncanonical scope and payload length in the message; it reads the largest canonical sequence number. The limits contract is run against a refused and an accepted record on each boundary above."
      "Zenoh Profile 0 links declared by a named configuration, with fragmentation when the component supplies the storage"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_links_check" { h.atLeast "negativeControlsRefused" 669; h.atMost "negativeControlsRefused" 1000; } "The checker refuses, before it runs the Rust tests, 669 corrupted records: 523 mutations of an honest transcript through the links judge, 91 through the host fragment reference, and 55 limits records through contracts/zenoh-link-limits/v1 out of 81 on its boundaries. The bound is inclusive at 669 so a checker that drops a control is caught; the upper bound is a sanity limit, not a target.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a13943-5c10-7fbd-b1e0-a1d4c2f89f28"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ac2b-753a-83fc-237fb9641377"
