    -- legacy 01a1514d-8af5-7fa1-a4c2-70be8785fb2e (done): Zenoh Profile 0 session taking a stock peer's undeclaration by subscriber id
    -- A stock eclipse-zenoh 1.0.0 peer, listening, ends the session it subscribed in by sending an
    -- UndeclareSubscriber that names the subscriber by id and nothing else, inside a DECLARE that carries
    -- the network QoS extension: the batch is 25 <sn> 9e 21 08 03 01. The codec leaves the wire expression
    -- out when it is null, so this is the encoder's ordinary output and not a quirk of one binding.
    -- Profile 0 refuses it. Its decoder takes an undeclaration only as header 0x83 with a wire-expression
    -- extension, refuses the QoS extension on one (refuse-qos-on-undeclare-subscriber), and refuses the
    -- bare 03 01 without the QoS (the pinned vector usub_missing_wire_expr_ext, 25011e0301, as malformed-
    -- message). The stock-peer exam captured a peer that never undeclared, so no capture held this batch.
    -- It surfaced when the guest of the external-listener exam published its four samples to a stock
    -- listener: the listener closed its subscription, the session refused the undeclaration, and the guest
    -- reported a link failure after the samples were on the wire. The upstream router removes a
    -- subscription by id and ignores the expression (hat/p2p_peer/pubsub.rs, forget_simple_subscription),
    -- so a key-less undeclaration is complete as sent.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ac78-753e-ac8a-cb2e80870fe5"
      "A connector session replays the eight batches a stock peer sent it, in the order sent, and takes each: its INIT_ACK, OPEN_ACK, OAM, DeclareKeyExpr, DeclareSubscriber with its DeclareFinal, KEEP_ALIVE, the undeclaration 25 <sn> 9e 21 08 03 01 and CLOSE. The undeclaration leaves the session with no remote subscriber and one SubscriberUndeclared event for id 1, and the CLOSE that follows closes it. The exam also runs the bare undeclaration and the full-form one the stock-peer exam already takes against a second session and requires the same state afterwards: no remote subscriber, the same sequence numbers, one event each."
      "Zenoh Profile 0 session taking a stock peer's undeclaration by subscriber id"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_undeclare_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 20; } "The checker counts the cases the Rust tests printed and the judge matched: the eight replayed batches and the two scenarios (10), and the ten refused variants by name and class (10), 20. The count is exact, not a floor: fewer means a batch or a refusal was not exercised, more means something ran that the exam does not name. It is reported only after the stock corpus judge, the retained suites and the stock-peer exam's tests passed beside it.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1514d-8af5-7fa1-a4c2-70be8785fb2e"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ac78-753e-ac8a-cb2ffd80ed63"
      "The host reference scripts/lib/zenoh_wire.py builds the captured undeclaration byte for byte: a reliable FRAME with the captured sequence number around undeclare_subscriber_by_id(1), which is DECLARE with the extension flag, the QoS extension 21 08, and the header 03 and the id. The exam does not take the capture on trust from the peer that wrote it. Six corrupted inputs to that check are refused, each for its own reason: a reference that undeclares another subscriber id, a captured subscriber that is id 2 and one through alias 2, a captured batch name used twice, a refused variant name used twice, and a refused variant that is a batch the peer sent."
      "Zenoh Profile 0 session taking a stock peer's undeclaration by subscriber id"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_undeclare_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 68; } "The checker refuses, before it runs any Rust, exactly 68 corrupted records: 44 transcripts through the exam's judge, 18 hand-off records through the contract's decoder and 6 corrupted inputs to the reference check. The count is exact: a checker that drops a control or invents one is caught, and a change to it is a re-admission.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1514d-8af5-7fa1-a4c2-70be8785fb2e"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ac78-753e-ac8a-cb309f72fba3"
      "Ten variants of the undeclaration, each built from it by one named change, are refused with the class they get: without the QoS (malformed-message), the full form behind the QoS (unsupported-extension), reserved header bit 5 and bit 6 (malformed-message), no id (truncated), an id over 32 bits (leb128-overflow), an id with a non-canonical encoding (leb128-noncanonical), a trailing byte after the message (unsupported-message), an id the session does not hold (unknown-subscriber) and the undeclaration repeated (unknown-subscriber). The decoder's classes were measured on the decoder with the change, not assumed."
      "Zenoh Profile 0 session taking a stock peer's undeclaration by subscriber id"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_undeclare_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 20; } "The checker counts the cases the Rust tests printed and the judge matched: the eight replayed batches and the two scenarios (10), and the ten refused variants by name and class (10), 20. The count is exact, not a floor: fewer means a batch or a refusal was not exercised, more means something ran that the exam does not name. It is reported only after the stock corpus judge, the retained suites and the stock-peer exam's tests passed beside it.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1514d-8af5-7fa1-a4c2-70be8785fb2e"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ac78-753e-ac8a-cb313e3d78ae"
      "The hand-off record is read only through contracts/zenoh-stock-undeclare/v1. The decoder accepts the honest record, and the same record spelled across several lines, and refuses 18: a missing group, format version 2 and 2 spelled across lines, a peer group and a refuse group of the wrong size, a name of 64 two-byte characters, odd-length and capital hex, a batch of 513 bytes, a row with no hex, hex that is not text, an unknown extra field at the top level, on the same line as a known one, on the opening line, inside an entry and over several lines, and a ninth peer entry and an eleventh refuse entry over several lines."
