    -- legacy 01a15d1f-26d2-7653-924b-a3f113a718e6 (done): Zenoh service grants: what each holder may publish and subscribe to
    -- The Zenoh service owns one link and serves several local holders, so it needs an authority model of
    -- its own. The fabric grants a route by a participant grant, and `network-application/v3` grants a
    -- destination by a row. Neither names a Zenoh key. A key string in a request must grant nothing, so a
    -- record must say which holder may publish or subscribe to which key. `contracts/zenoh-service-
    -- grants/v1` is that record, and no exam has exercised it yet.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-acad-760a-9132-55881bc7d324"
      "The contract takes the honest record of three holders, four 12-byte ring slots, three local subscriptions and five rows."
      "Zenoh service grants: what each holder may publish and subscribe to"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_grants_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 68; } "The checker counts 17 declarations that the contract takes, 42 that it refuses and 9 constants, 68 in all. The count is exact, because a bound that is not held changes it. It is reported only after the generated constants equal the schema's.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a15d1f-26d2-7653-924b-a3f113a718e6"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-acad-760a-9132-55890d00fd62"
      "The contract takes a stack of exactly what the declaration needs and refuses a stack one byte short."
