    -- legacy 01a15d1f-2e50-7f0f-9721-ce4b3b5f5aa8 (done): Zenoh service core: one session served to local holders by their grants
    -- A Zenoh service core does not exist, and nothing says what serving a holder means. Four rules are
    -- undecided in code. The keys that holders may subscribe to are declared to the peer once the session
    -- is open. A publication reaches every local holder with a subscribe grant, and goes to the peer only
    -- if the peer declared the key. A peer's sample reaches every holder subscribed to its key and no
    -- other. A holder that does not drain its ring never blocks another and never grows a queue. The
    -- session cannot support this yet, because it holds one subscription of its own and does not say which
    -- subscription matched a sample. This item judges the core on the host before any component exists.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-acba-7098-b20d-82cc1552e1de"
      "The core is declared with three holders, four ring slots, 12 sample bytes, three local subscriptions and five rows."
      "Zenoh service core: one session served to local holders by their grants"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 59; } "The checker counts 47 lines that the Rust test printed. They are sizes, constants, frames, scenarios, publications, deliveries, counts and losses. It also counts 12 refusals by name and class. The total is 59. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the subscribers, links and stock-peer exams pass.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a15d1f-2e50-7f0f-9721-ce4b3b5f5aa8"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-acba-7098-b20d-82cd11c6fbc2"
      "The Rust test prints the size of a slot, a row, a holder and the core. Each is at most the matching overhead constant in the grants contract."
      "Zenoh service core: one session served to local holders by their grants"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 59; } "The checker counts 47 lines that the Rust test printed. They are sizes, constants, frames, scenarios, publications, deliveries, counts and losses. It also counts 12 refusals by name and class. The total is 59. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the subscribers, links and stock-peer exams pass.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a15d1f-2e50-7f0f-9721-ce4b3b5f5aa8"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-acba-7098-b20d-82ced4d68e17"
      "After the session opens, the core writes subscription 1 for `k1` and subscription 2 for `k2`, and the peer takes both."
      "Zenoh service core: one session served to local holders by their grants"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 59; } "The checker counts 47 lines that the Rust test printed. They are sizes, constants, frames, scenarios, publications, deliveries, counts and losses. It also counts 12 refusals by name and class. The total is 59. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the subscribers, links and stock-peer exams pass.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a15d1f-2e50-7f0f-9721-ce4b3b5f5aa8"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-acba-7098-b20d-82cf40cc10d4"
      "The host reference reproduces both declaration frames and both publication frames byte for byte."
      "Zenoh service core: one session served to local holders by their grants"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 59; } "The checker counts 47 lines that the Rust test printed. They are sizes, constants, frames, scenarios, publications, deliveries, counts and losses. It also counts 12 refusals by name and class. The total is 59. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the subscribers, links and stock-peer exams pass.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a15d1f-2e50-7f0f-9721-ce4b3b5f5aa8"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-acba-7098-b20d-82d025b69711"
      "A publication by `a` on `k1` before the peer declares it reaches `a` and `b` and is reported as not subscribed."
