      "`just zenoh_service_check` passes as the gate adapter observes it, and it fails naming the test that did not pass until the core lands."
      "Zenoh service core: one session served to local holders by their grants"
      {
        h.observedWhere "recipe-passed" "zenoh_service_check" h.noPredicates "The gate adapter reports the recipe's exit code, so the checker cannot vouch for itself.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a15d1f-2e50-7f0f-9721-ce4b3b5f5aa8"; }; };
    -- legacy 01a17dad-f158-7efd-bea7-dfdf0288432b (done): Run the Zenoh service core over a link
    -- The Zenoh service core borrows a bare session, and a component cannot use that. A component owns a
    -- link, and the link owns the session, one send slot, retries and keep-alives. Four rules are
    -- undecided in code. A declaration or a publication must go through the link's single send slot. A
    -- second call while the slot is taken must be refused, with nothing changed. This holds for the same
    -- operation and for the other one. Local copies of a publication must reach the rings only after the
    -- link handed the frame to the byte stream. A peer's sample must reach the holders by the subscription
    -- that matched. A byte stream can take a frame and then reset, and the core cannot know whether the
    -- peer received it. This item judges the core over a link on the host before any component exists.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ad53-701c-816c-88c155775b14"
      "The core is declared with three holders, four ring slots, 12 sample bytes and three local subscriptions. The link holds eight notices. The core has the five grant rows of the service core."
      "Run the Zenoh service core over a link"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_link_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 61; } "The checker counts 44 lines that the Rust test printed. They are sizes, frames, scenarios, publications, deliveries, counts and losses. It also counts 17 refusals by name and class. The total is 61. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the subscribers, links and stock-peer exams pass.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a17dad-f158-7efd-bea7-dfdf0288432b"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ad53-701c-816c-88c22fc98261"
      "The Rust test prints the size of a slot, a row, a holder and the core. Each is at most the matching overhead constant in the grants contract."
      "Run the Zenoh service core over a link"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_link_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 61; } "The checker counts 44 lines that the Rust test printed. They are sizes, frames, scenarios, publications, deliveries, counts and losses. It also counts 17 refusals by name and class. The total is 61. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the subscribers, links and stock-peer exams pass.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a17dad-f158-7efd-bea7-dfdf0288432b"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ad53-701c-816c-88c319af5649"
      "The core queues subscription 1, then finds the send slot taken. It refuses a second declaration and a publication as `busy`. It counts subscription 1 as declared only after the flush. Subscription 2 follows the same way."
      "Run the Zenoh service core over a link"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_link_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 61; } "The checker counts 44 lines that the Rust test printed. They are sizes, frames, scenarios, publications, deliveries, counts and losses. It also counts 17 refusals by name and class. The total is 61. The count is exact, and it is reported only after the subscribers, links and stock-peer exams pass.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a17dad-f158-7efd-bea7-dfdf0288432b"; }; };
