    -- legacy 01a195e7-b4e9-708e-a266-6cf708d4f35a (done): Build the Zenoh service grants table in the generation builder
    -- The Zenoh service grants table has an encoder, and nothing calls it. The generation builder turns a
    -- system spec into a generation, and it has no step that builds the table from the grants a spec
    -- declares. Without that step, the table cannot reach the root. The first system spec to declare
    -- grants would also be the first test of the code that carries them. This item adds the builder step
    -- and the spec admission that runs it. It also adds a judge that grades both against the encoder's
    -- bytes and an independent writer.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-adfd-7183-9e8c-8df8f106c335"
      "From a manifest with three rows and a `zenoh-service` instance, the builder emits the bytes that `zenoh_grants_table.encode` emits. They equal the bytes that the table judge's struct writer emits, and they decode to the declared rows. Reversing the rows and the instances gives the same bytes."
      "Build the Zenoh service grants table in the generation builder"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_grants_builder_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 7; } "The checker counts seven checks that the builder's output must pass. Four compare the output with the encoder, with the independent writer, with a decode back to the rows and with a reversed order. Three follow a valid spec through admission. The count is exact. It is reported only after all seven held.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a195e7-b4e9-708e-a266-6cf708d4f35a"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-adfd-7183-9e8c-8df936a1932e"
      "The builder refuses eleven manifests. Four concern the manifest: no rows, no reader instance, a holder that is not an instance, and the reader as a holder. Seven concern a row: it grants nothing, its key has a wildcard or is 130 bytes, or it repeats a pair. A row may also hold a field the grants record lacks, lack its key, or carry rights that are not booleans. Each is refused at the boundary that owns it."
      "Build the Zenoh service grants table in the generation builder"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_grants_builder_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 14; } "The checker refuses exactly 14 inputs. Eleven are manifests and three are specs. Each names the boundary that must refuse it, so an input refused by another boundary fails the exam. A one-line mutation of each builder check was run against the slice. One removed check, the empty table, is also refused by the encoder, so removing it from the builder changes the message and not the verdict.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a195e7-b4e9-708e-a266-6cf708d4f35a"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-adfd-7183-9e8c-8dfa2a85b707"
      "A real spec with a `zenoh-service` instance added and three grants set is admitted. The manifest it derives holds the three rows as declared and a `zenoh-grants` object. The table built from that manifest equals the encoder's bytes for the rows. A derivation that dropped every row, or kept only the first, fails the slice."
      "Build the Zenoh service grants table in the generation builder"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_grants_builder_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 7; } "The checker counts seven checks that the builder's output must pass. Four compare the output with the encoder, with the independent writer, with a decode back to the rows and with a reversed order. Three follow a valid spec through admission. The count is exact. It is reported only after all seven held.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a195e7-b4e9-708e-a266-6cf708d4f35a"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-adfe-7113-80ba-20c4788e2131"
      "The system spec refuses three specs. They are grants without their object, a holder the spec does not admit and an object with no grants. The two new keys default in, so every existing spec is accepted as before."
      "Build the Zenoh service grants table in the generation builder"
