    -- legacy 01a19add-bddf-77a3-ab9c-ca12ecb6512f (done): A hash-pinned frame store read from a read-only QEMU disk
    -- The LiDAR frame store from 01a18064-a82b-70cb-bb32-527657addf86 is about 99 MB and is converted from
    -- a bag that is not committed, so no system-image closure can carry it, and building it into a
    -- generation would make every recording a new image. A run can attach it as a disk instead: system-
    -- test-run records already declare disks, virtio-blk-driver serves block rings whose rights and sector
    -- range the generation declares, and one block request moves 4 KiB. Nothing defines how a payload sits
    -- on such a disk, nothing writes that disk from a frame store, and no guest component reads one back.
    -- This item replaces 01a18064-bd3b-790e-8606-762289dbb197, which would have built the data into the
    -- image.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae17-7392-a485-e1ed24645d49"
      "build-data-volume.py writes, for the exam's frame store and for components/lib/src/frame_store/fixture.bin, exactly the disk the exam computes from the contract, and refuses an unknown kind as kind, a payload that is not a frame store as payload and an existing output as output, leaving no new file and the existing output unchanged."
      "A hash-pinned frame store read from a read-only QEMU disk"
      {
        h.observedWhere "data-volume-observed" "data_volume_check" h.noPredicates "data_volume_check compares the builder's disks byte for byte with an independent encoder of the contract, builds the image through build-system-image.py, and boots it with the honest disk and seven disks it corrupted itself. The probe hashes the bytes it read and the driver reports the authority it enforced, so a probe that skipped a check, lost a frame or never wrote prints a line the judge refuses.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19add-bddf-77a3-ab9c-ca12ecb6512f"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae17-7392-a485-e1ee442c4f83"
      "sel4-data-volume boots on aarch64 QEMU with the builder's disk of the exam's frame store attached read-only. data-volume-probe prints the payload's byte count and SHA-256, then the frame count, period, first and last log time and the SHA-256 of the payloads in index order, then a refused write, a heap use of at most 65536 bytes, and completion. Before the probe reports the refused write, virtio-blk-driver reports that its one ring has read rights only and that it refused one write on ring 0."
      "A hash-pinned frame store read from a read-only QEMU disk"
      {
        h.observedWhere "data-volume-observed" "data_volume_check" h.noPredicates "data_volume_check compares the builder's disks byte for byte with an independent encoder of the contract, builds the image through build-system-image.py, and boots it with the honest disk and seven disks it corrupted itself. The probe hashes the bytes it read and the driver reports the authority it enforced, so a probe that skipped a check, lost a frame or never wrote prints a line the judge refuses.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19add-bddf-77a3-ab9c-ca12ecb6512f"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae17-7392-a485-e1ef5150ab46"
      "Seven disks, each built to fail one check of the contract first (a GPT header, the partition type, the volume header, the payload length, the padding after the payload, the payload hash, and the frame store), are each refused by the probe with that check's class and nothing printed after it; only the frame-store refusal follows the volume line."
      "A hash-pinned frame store read from a read-only QEMU disk"
      {
        h.observedWhere "data-volume-observed" "data_volume_check" h.noPredicates "data_volume_check compares the builder's disks byte for byte with an independent encoder of the contract, builds the image through build-system-image.py, and boots it with the honest disk and seven disks it corrupted itself. The probe hashes the bytes it read and the driver reports the authority it enforced, so a probe that skipped a check, lost a frame or never wrote prints a line the judge refuses.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19add-bddf-77a3-ab9c-ca12ecb6512f"; }; };
    -- legacy 01a19c28-eaeb-7f64-846a-502f03dc2688 (done): Plan the Zenoh grants reader: the read label, the schema fields, the root reader and the wrapper
    -- The Zenoh grants table is built by the generation builder and nothing in the root reads it. A Zenoh
    -- service component needs the root to serve the table to it, and a spec author needs the two spec keys
    -- in the schema. Both are product changes, so this item plans them and a later pull request implements
    -- them. This item adds the exam that grades the product side. The exam fails until the implementation
    -- lands.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae26-71d0-984f-71474e5d13e1"
      "The contract declares `ZENOH_GRANTS_READ` as capability table label 75, the highest used label being 74. Its Rust and C outputs and its documentation row carry it. The manifest schema declares `ZenohGrantEntry` with `holder`, `key`, `publish` and `subscribe`, and the optional field `zenohGrants`. The system spec schema declares the same record, the field `zenohGrants`, the flag `zenohGrantsObject` and the bound `maxZenohGrants` of 64. The bound reaches the generated Python constant and the ceiling entry."
      "Plan the Zenoh grants reader: the read label, the schema fields, the root reader and the wrapper"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_grants_reader_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 36; } "The checker counts 36 cases. Thirty-five are declarations that the product files must hold. One is the filtered run of the two reader tests. The count is exact and is reported only after all of them held. The declarations are text and show that the code exists. The tests show what the reader does.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c28-eaeb-7f64-846a-502f03dc2688"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae26-71d0-984f-7148dca09a3a"
      "The `slime-root` reader locates the resource object by the table's magic and serves 168-byte rows only to the instance named `zenoh-service`. A dispatch arm, a route entry and a route test entry carry the label. The wrapper in `components/runtime` calls the label and returns the count of rows."
      "Plan the Zenoh grants reader: the read label, the schema fields, the root reader and the wrapper"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_grants_reader_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 36; } "The checker counts 36 cases. Thirty-five are declarations that the product files must hold. One is the filtered run of the two reader tests. The count is exact and is reported only after all of them held. The declarations are text and show that the code exists. The tests show what the reader does.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c28-eaeb-7f64-846a-502f03dc2688"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae26-71d0-984f-714939c805d4"
      "Two `slime-root` tests run alone and pass. One shows the rows go only to `zenoh-service`. The other shows paging by row cursor within the staged bound of 1024 bytes, which is 6 rows per call. The run filters out exactly 363 tests, and the pin in `just/quality.just` is 365."
      "Plan the Zenoh grants reader: the read label, the schema fields, the root reader and the wrapper"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_grants_reader_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 36; } "The checker counts 36 cases. Thirty-five are declarations that the product files must hold. One is the filtered run of the two reader tests. The count is exact and is reported only after all of them held. The declarations are text and show that the code exists. The tests show what the reader does.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c28-eaeb-7f64-846a-502f03dc2688"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae26-71d0-984f-714aa4e823b6"
      "The exam refuses 41 inputs. Thirty-five remove one declaration from a synthetic file set, and the exam must refuse by naming that declaration. Six alter the transcript of the filtered run. The six are a run of no test, a third test, a failed test and a test of another name. The last two are a count that does not add up and two runs in one output."
      "Plan the Zenoh grants reader: the read label, the schema fields, the root reader and the wrapper"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_grants_reader_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 41; } "The checker refuses exactly 41 inputs. Each declaration is removed from a synthetic file set in turn, and the refusal must name it. A declaration that another one also matches would be accepted, and the exam would not run. Six alterations of the test transcript are refused as well. The unaltered corpus and transcript are accepted first.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c28-eaeb-7f64-846a-502f03dc2688"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae26-71d0-984f-714be4b4dd88"
      "`just zenoh_service_grants_reader_check` exits zero and reports its observations through the gate adapter. It fails on `main` until the implementation lands."
      "Plan the Zenoh grants reader: the read label, the schema fields, the root reader and the wrapper"
      {
        h.observedWhere "recipe-passed" "zenoh_service_grants_reader_check" h.noPredicates "The gate adapter reports the recipe's exit code, so the checker cannot vouch for itself. The recipe passes only after the implementation pull request merges, because the full run reads the product files.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c28-eaeb-7f64-846a-502f03dc2688"; }; };
    -- legacy 01a19c28-f3cf-729b-bd18-d0a116e1ca91 (done): Plan the Zenoh service server half of the client protocol
    -- The Zenoh service client adapter exists and nothing answers it. The service side of the protocol
    -- must take a holder's request, ask the service core, and return the completion the client checks.
    -- This item plans that server half as plain Rust in the component library, so a host test can drive
    -- it. It adds the exam that grades the server half against bytes the judge writes itself. The exam
    -- fails until the implementation lands.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae34-74d2-baf4-ab1d30356c73"
      "Each completion the server returns equals the bytes that `struct` writes from `completionLayout`. Each sample header in the data page equals the bytes written from `sampleHeaderLayout`. The server stamps the timestamp from the time it is given."
      "Plan the Zenoh service server half of the client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_server_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 39; } "The checker counts 39 lines. Twenty-four are honest answers and 15 are refusals. The count is exact. It is reported only after every line matched the bytes the judge wrote. The Rust test prints what the server answered, and the judge never reads the Rust.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c28-f3cf-729b-bd18-d0a116e1ca91"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae34-74d2-baf4-ab1e50236979"
      "A publication on a key reaches every holder with a subscribe row on it, the publisher included. A holder with no publish row on the key is denied, and so is a holder with no rows. A refused publication reaches no ring. A holder that attaches twice is denied."
      "Plan the Zenoh service server half of the client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_server_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 39; } "The checker counts 39 lines. Twenty-four are honest answers and 15 are refusals. The count is exact. It is reported only after every line matched the bytes the judge wrote. The Rust test prints what the server answered, and the judge never reads the Rust.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c28-f3cf-729b-bd18-d0a116e1ca91"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae34-74d2-baf4-ab1fe3015eed"
      "A full ring drops its oldest sample and says so once, before the samples that remain. A take into a buffer smaller than the next sample is refused and the sample stays. After a detach or an abort the holder has no session."
      "Plan the Zenoh service server half of the client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_server_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 39; } "The checker counts 39 lines. Twenty-four are honest answers and 15 are refusals. The count is exact. It is reported only after every line matched the bytes the judge wrote. The Rust test prints what the server answered, and the judge never reads the Rust.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c28-f3cf-729b-bd18-d0a116e1ca91"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae34-74d2-baf4-ab208d112e7b"
      "No completion the exam lists is one the client refuses. A failure carries its status and nothing else. A request outside the protocol is answered with the operation it names and changes nothing."
      "Plan the Zenoh service server half of the client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_server_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 39; } "The checker counts 39 lines. Twenty-four are honest answers and 15 are refusals. The count is exact. It is reported only after every line matched the bytes the judge wrote. The Rust test prints what the server answered, and the judge never reads the Rust.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c28-f3cf-729b-bd18-d0a116e1ca91"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae34-74d2-baf4-ab21afa0707a"
      "The exam refuses 104 inputs. Eighty-five remove or change one line of the transcript. Fifteen break a rule the client applies to a completion, and that includes a publish refusal that does not echo its row. Four corrupt the schema's layout, and the honest transcript must then be refused."
      "Plan the Zenoh service server half of the client protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_server_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 104; } "The checker refuses exactly 104 inputs. Each one changes the transcript, the client's rules or the layout, and the judge must refuse it. The unaltered transcript is accepted first.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19c28-f3cf-729b-bd18-d0a116e1ca91"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae34-74d2-baf4-ab2220b92f5d"
