    -- legacy 01a19cdb-5986-7d5f-a948-0d23122f52e5 (done): A guest publisher reads the LiDAR frames from a read-only disk and sends them over Zenoh to a host peer
    -- The only guest Zenoh publisher, ros2-demo-publisher-external in sel4-zenoh-external, sends four
    -- fixed 12-byte Counter samples in whole frames and stops. The LiDAR frame store, 200 PointCloud2
    -- frames of 494,889 bytes each, now reaches a guest on a read-only data volume (01a19add-
    -- bddf-77a3-ab9c-ca12ecb6512f). Its components/lib reader only validates the volume, and no component
    -- reads a frame back out. A finite plane's root stops after 131072 component arrivals, fewer than one
    -- pass over that disk costs. Network-service carries at most 4096 bytes per data operation, so each
    -- frame crosses as about 121 batches. The stock eclipse-zenoh 1.0.0 peer the external Zenoh checks use
    -- is pinned for x86-64 Linux only. This item supersedes 01a18064-d302-7eb7-98d7-dcf45cc34077, which
    -- would have carried the store in the image.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae68-720d-8a47-df998ddbd7fd"
      "In one boot with one pass, the host peer's record holds exactly the store's frame count of samples on the key. Sample i has frame i's payload length and SHA-256 and the attachment for sequence i + 1, frame i's log time and the demo GID. Every Put the capture carries reassembles to the same key, attachment and frame i's payload byte for byte, in order."
      "A guest publisher reads the LiDAR frames from a read-only disk and sends them over Zenoh to a host peer"
      {
        h.observedWhere "lidar-publish-observed" "lidar_publish_check" h.noPredicates "lidar_publish_check judges what a stock Zenoh peer received and what the capture at the guest's device carried against a store the exam encodes from the hash-pinned bag, so the guest cannot report its way to a pass. The period bound is a lower bound only, which a slow emulator cannot fail by being slow. Throughput, late frames and elapsed time are printed as observations.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19cdb-5986-7d5f-a948-0d23122f52e5"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae68-720d-8a47-df9ab6b8816c"
      "In the capture, the first packet carrying Put i + 1 is at least the 500 ms period minus 5 ms after the first packet carrying Put i. The publisher reports the store's frame count, period and payload digest, then a summary whose frames and bytes equal the store's totals, then that the session closed."
      "A guest publisher reads the LiDAR frames from a read-only disk and sends them over Zenoh to a host peer"
      {
        h.observedWhere "lidar-publish-observed" "lidar_publish_check" h.noPredicates "lidar_publish_check judges what a stock Zenoh peer received and what the capture at the guest's device carried against a store the exam encodes from the hash-pinned bag, so the guest cannot report its way to a pass. The period bound is a lower bound only, which a slow emulator cannot fail by being slow. Throughput, late frames and elapsed time are printed as observations.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19cdb-5986-7d5f-a948-0d23122f52e5"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae68-720d-8a47-df9b895f93f2"
      "The capture holds exactly one TCP connection, from the guest to 10.0.2.2:17447, closed by both sides without a reset, and no other IPv4 traffic. Every Zenoh batch the guest sends is at most 4096 bytes including its stream length prefix."
      "A guest publisher reads the LiDAR frames from a read-only disk and sends them over Zenoh to a host peer"
      {
        h.observedWhere "lidar-publish-observed" "lidar_publish_check" h.noPredicates "lidar_publish_check judges what a stock Zenoh peer received and what the capture at the guest's device carried against a store the exam encodes from the hash-pinned bag, so the guest cannot report its way to a pass. The period bound is a lower bound only, which a slow emulator cannot fail by being slow. Throughput, late frames and elapsed time are printed as observations.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19cdb-5986-7d5f-a948-0d23122f52e5"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae68-720d-8a47-df9cc27ee972"
      "The root reports the arrival ceiling sel4-lidar-external's system spec declares, above 131072, once before the publisher's first line. The boot ends SLIME_GRAPH HEALTHY with failed=0 after the publisher reports the session closed, with no failure line and no exhausted arrival ceiling."
      "A guest publisher reads the LiDAR frames from a read-only disk and sends them over Zenoh to a host peer"
      {
        h.observedWhere "lidar-publish-observed" "lidar_publish_check" h.noPredicates "lidar_publish_check judges what a stock Zenoh peer received and what the capture at the guest's device carried against a store the exam encodes from the hash-pinned bag, so the guest cannot report its way to a pass. The period bound is a lower bound only, which a slow emulator cannot fail by being slow. Throughput, late frames and elapsed time are printed as observations.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a19cdb-5986-7d5f-a948-0d23122f52e5"; }; };
    -- legacy 01a1a43b-cb66-7d19-8b91-12240b7e1e74 (done): A host bridge forwards the LiDAR Zenoh topic to Foxglove over the SDK WebSocket protocol
    -- Foxglove reads live data over its WebSocket protocol; the guest speaks Zenoh. Nothing in the
    -- repository connects the two, so a frame lidar-publisher sends cannot be shown in Foxglove. A ROS 2
    -- install with rmw_zenoh and foxglove_bridge would need ROS graph discovery, which the guest's Profile
    -- 0 does not provide. Foxglove marks its foxglove.websocket.v1 specification outdated and serves
    -- foxglove.sdk.v1 from its SDK. This item supersedes 01a18064-e788-7b41-ba54-2b84c152dea9, which
    -- placed the bridge under scripts/, the grader tree.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae86-739a-ab9c-f7380b94edf5"
      "A client offering the foxglove.sdk.v1 subprotocol completes the WebSocket handshake with it. It receives server info and exactly one channel advertisement. That channel has the store's topic, encoding cdr, the store's type as schema name, schema encoding ros2msg and the store's schema text byte for byte."
      "A host bridge forwards the LiDAR Zenoh topic to Foxglove over the SDK WebSocket protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "bridge-observed" "lidar_foxglove_bridge_check" h.noPredicates "lidar_foxglove_bridge_check drives the bridge from a stock Zenoh replayer and judges it from an independent client of the Foxglove protocol, comparing every payload and log time with the frame store, so the bridge cannot pass by reporting on itself. It needs no QEMU.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1a43b-cb66-7d19-8b91-12240b7e1e74"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae86-739a-ab9c-f7390ed3660a"
      "After the client subscribes, the replayer publishes the converted LiDAR store's 200 frames on the store's data key, each with its rmw_zenoh attachment. The client receives exactly 200 message-data frames on its subscription. Message i's payload equals frame i's payload byte for byte, in order, and its log time equals frame i's log time."
      "A host bridge forwards the LiDAR Zenoh topic to Foxglove over the SDK WebSocket protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "bridge-observed" "lidar_foxglove_bridge_check" h.noPredicates "lidar_foxglove_bridge_check drives the bridge from a stock Zenoh replayer and judges it from an independent client of the Foxglove protocol, comparing every payload and log time with the frame store, so the bridge cannot pass by reporting on itself. It needs no QEMU.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1a43b-cb66-7d19-8b91-12240b7e1e74"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-ae86-739a-ab9c-f73aab77f68d"
      "Started with one pinned wheel's hash changed, the bridge exits nonzero with a final stderr line foxglove-bridge: refused dependency and listens on neither port. A sample on another key under domain 0 reaches no client and is counted on one drop line."
      "A host bridge forwards the LiDAR Zenoh topic to Foxglove over the SDK WebSocket protocol"
      {
        h.observedWhere "bridge-observed" "lidar_foxglove_bridge_check" h.noPredicates "lidar_foxglove_bridge_check drives the bridge from a stock Zenoh replayer and judges it from an independent client of the Foxglove protocol, comparing every payload and log time with the frame store, so the bridge cannot pass by reporting on itself. It needs no QEMU.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1a43b-cb66-7d19-8b91-12240b7e1e74"; }; };
    -- legacy 01a1a8cb-a7a0-7dc1-bb24-951d0db30d1e (done): The recorded LiDAR cloud reaches Foxglove from a SlimeOS guest through the bridge
    -- The LiDAR publisher (01a19cdb-5986-7d5f-a948-0d23122f52e5) and the Foxglove bridge
    -- (01a1a43b-cb66-7d19-8b91-12240b7e1e74) were judged apart: one against a stock peer that subscribes
    -- the exact data key, the other against a stock replayer. Joined, the guest refuses the bridge: the
    -- bridge subscribes 0/**, the guest's Profile 0 session refuses a wildcard key declaration, and lidar-
    -- publisher fails with link session refused before its first frame. With the bridge subscribed to the
    -- store's exact data key, the same boot delivers all 200 frames and ends HEALTHY. Nothing yet shows
    -- the recorded point cloud leaving a SlimeOS guest and arriving in Foxglove, which is the demo the
    -- owner asked for. This item supersedes 01a18064-fb47-7821-a2e3-2d81962df0bc, which did not name the
    -- bridge's subscription.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aea9-7498-9c95-282d750c93c5"
      "In lidar_foxglove_bridge_check, the replayer's sample on another key under domain 0 reaches no client. The client receives exactly the store's 200 frames in order, and the bridge prints exactly its ready line and foxglove-bridge: stopped forwarded=200."
      "The recorded LiDAR cloud reaches Foxglove from a SlimeOS guest through the bridge"
      {
        h.observedWhere "bridge-observed" "lidar_foxglove_demo_check" h.noPredicates "lidar_foxglove_bridge_check drives the bridge from a stock Zenoh replayer and judges it from an independent Foxglove client, so a sample on another key that reached the client, or a drop the bridge reported, fails it.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1a8cb-a7a0-7dc1-bb24-951d0db30d1e"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aea9-7498-9c95-282e4107cea0"
      "In one boot with one pass, the client receives the bridge's channel advertisement for /velodyne_points and then exactly 200 message-data frames whose payloads and log times equal the frame store's, in order. The guest reports the store, a summary equal to it and the closed session, the capture holds one TCP connection to 10.0.2.2:17447, and the boot ends HEALTHY."
      "The recorded LiDAR cloud reaches Foxglove from a SlimeOS guest through the bridge"
      {
        h.observedWhere "demo-observed" "lidar_foxglove_demo_check" h.noPredicates "lidar_foxglove_demo_check runs the whole chain, guest publisher through network-service and the bridge, and judges it from an independent Foxglove protocol client against the hash-pinned frame store. A bridge whose subscription the guest refuses fails it.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1a8cb-a7a0-7dc1-bb24-951d0db30d1e"; }; };
    (h.planned "01a1b49c-aea9-7498-9c95-282ff7237538"
      "The owner opened the manual demo's URL in Foxglove and saw the point cloud update on /velodyne_points."
      "The recorded LiDAR cloud reaches Foxglove from a SlimeOS guest through the bridge"
      "rehomed from a done item; only a human gate: needs an automated exam"
      {
        h.human "demo-viewed" "lidar-foxglove-viewed" "Seeing the cloud render is a human observation no checker can make; it is recorded only with the owner's explicit confirmation.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1a8cb-a7a0-7dc1-bb24-951d0db30d1e"; }; };
    -- legacy 01a1af02-029f-7e62-a3b4-91b37d965b84 (done): Plan the Zenoh service limits record and the sizes it checks
    -- The Zenoh service sizes its core with constants of its own, two holders and two rows, and the core
    -- refuses any table of another size. The grants record declares six limits, and the generation carries
    -- none of them. This item plans a limits record that the generation carries and the root serves. The
    -- service checks the record against what it was built to hold. The exam fails until the implementation
    -- lands.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aec1-760f-a2b8-9a015acc6fe4"
      "The contract states a 48-byte record of the six limits. The exam writes the same bytes with struct from a layout pinned in the exam. It requires the generated Rust binding to equal the renderer's output. It refuses 17 edits of the schema, 3 edits that move a field the encoder reads and 11 edits of the binding."
      "Plan the Zenoh service limits record and the sizes it checks"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_limits_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 36; } "The checker counts ${CASES} cases: 7 honest limit sets, 25 declarations the files must hold and 4 bounds on optional fields. A pattern shows that a call appears in a file and does not show what the code does. Behaviour is checked in the implementation review and by the booted composition.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1af02-029f-7e62-a3b4-91b37d965b84"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aec1-760f-a2b8-9a0233b6cce1"
      "The encoder refuses each limit of zero and each limit above its bound. It refuses a negative limit, a boolean, text or a float in a limit, a missing limit, an extra field and no fields. The exam refuses 19 such inputs."
      "Plan the Zenoh service limits record and the sizes it checks"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_limits_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 113; } "The checker refuses exactly ${CONTROLS} inputs. Each is applied alone, and the unaltered input is accepted first. No two controls corrupt the same input in the same way. The stack has no above-bound record.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1af02-029f-7e62-a3b4-91b37d965b84"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aec1-760f-a2b8-9a03db01b103"
      "A decoder written in the exam refuses 20 corruptions of an honest record. They cover its length, magic, version, size and flags. They also cover each limit at zero and each limit but the stack above its bound. The stack bound is the largest value four bytes hold, so no record is above it."
      "Plan the Zenoh service limits record and the sizes it checks"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_limits_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 113; } "The checker refuses exactly ${CONTROLS} inputs. Each is applied alone, and the unaltered input is accepted first. No two controls corrupt the same input in the same way. The stack has no above-bound record.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1af02-029f-7e62-a3b4-91b37d965b84"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aec1-760f-a2b8-9a049b07d259"
      "The system spec and the manifest declare all six limits on the service's instance. The system spec carries them to the manifest instance and derives the object from them, so it has no flag. It refuses limits on any other instance. The generation builder installs the object `zenoh-limits`. The closure release inputs, and the closure schema checker's list, carry the exact names `zenoh-limits-contract`, `zenoh-limits-encoder` and `generation-resources`."
      "Plan the Zenoh service limits record and the sizes it checks"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_limits_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 36; } "The checker counts ${CASES} cases: 7 honest limit sets, 25 declarations the files must hold and 4 bounds on optional fields. A pattern shows that a call appears in a file and does not show what the code does. Behaviour is checked in the implementation review and by the booted composition.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1af02-029f-7e62-a3b4-91b37d965b84"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aec1-760f-a2b8-9a050a11b9d3"
      "The root locates the object. The dispatch in `graph_runtime/services.rs` has its own branch for the cursor 4294967295 and returns the 48-byte record, and no row. The exam requires the locate and the branch by pattern."
      "Plan the Zenoh service limits record and the sizes it checks"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_limits_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 36; } "The checker counts ${CASES} cases: 7 honest limit sets, 25 declarations the files must hold and 4 bounds on optional fields. A pattern shows that a call appears in a file and does not show what the code does. Behaviour is checked in the implementation review and by the booted composition.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1af02-029f-7e62-a3b4-91b37d965b84"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aec1-760f-a2b8-9a06c739aad4"
      "The service reads the record before the rows and decodes it with the generated binding. The exam requires the read by pattern. What the service does with an over-ceiling record, and what the core accepts, are for the implementation review."
      "Plan the Zenoh service limits record and the sizes it checks"
