      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1af02-029f-7e62-a3b4-91b37d965b84"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aec1-760f-a2b8-9a070f34561f"
      "The exam refuses ${CONTROLS} inputs. 59 are in the encoder and the record, and 11 are in the binding. 8 are imports in the encoder. 25 each remove one declaration from a synthetic file set. 10 each add a field to one record."
      "Plan the Zenoh service limits record and the sizes it checks"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_limits_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 113; } "The checker refuses exactly ${CONTROLS} inputs. Each is applied alone, and the unaltered input is accepted first. No two controls corrupt the same input in the same way. The stack has no above-bound record.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1af02-029f-7e62-a3b4-91b37d965b84"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aec1-760f-a2b8-9a0852adf7b7"
      "`just zenoh_service_limits_check` exits zero and reports its observations through the gate adapter. It fails on `main` until the implementation lands."
      "Plan the Zenoh service limits record and the sizes it checks"
      {
        h.observedWhere "recipe-passed" "zenoh_service_limits_check" h.noPredicates "The gate adapter reports the recipe's exit code, so the checker cannot vouch for itself. The recipe passes only after the implementation pull request merges, because the full run reads the files it names.";
