    -- legacy 01a1af02-1d8b-7a48-9b9f-84747d5a4f72 (done): Plan the Zenoh limits builder checks and the rows they hold to the record
    -- The generation builder encodes the Zenoh service limits record and never compares the rows with it.
    -- A manifest whose limits declare one holder, or short keys, is accepted beside rows that name more
    -- holders and longer keys. The service then serves more than the declaration says. This item plans the
    -- builder's checks and the exam that grades them. The exam fails until the implementation lands.
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aecf-703a-b540-2c6abecf3591"
      "The builder emits the encoder's bytes for a manifest's limits. The exam requires the independent struct writer's bytes and a decode back to the declared limits, whatever order the rows and instances come in."
      "Plan the Zenoh limits builder checks and the rows they hold to the record"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_limits_builder_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 13; } "The checker counts ${CASES} honest checks. Four are the record's bytes, three ways and one reorder. Six hold the limits at the rows. Three are exact. One has a key that is not subscribed, one has two holders on one key, and one has a stack below the executable's. Three are of the record a spec derives. A builder that emits other bytes or refuses at a limit fails.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1af02-1d8b-7a48-9b9f-84747d5a4f72"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aecf-703a-b540-2c6b53163abc"
      "The builder refuses rows that name more holders than the record declares. It refuses rows that subscribe to more distinct keys than it declares, or hold a key longer than it declares. The exam holds each limit exactly at the rows, and with a key that is published and not subscribed."
      "Plan the Zenoh limits builder checks and the rows they hold to the record"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_limits_builder_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 13; } "The checker counts ${CASES} honest checks. Four are the record's bytes, three ways and one reorder. Six hold the limits at the rows. Three are exact. One has a key that is not subscribed, one has two holders on one key, and one has a stack below the executable's. Three are of the record a spec derives. A builder that emits other bytes or refuses at a limit fails.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1af02-1d8b-7a48-9b9f-84747d5a4f72"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aecf-703a-b540-2c6c18ed229a"
      "A spec that declares the service and its limits derives a manifest whose service instance holds the limits as declared and the object `zenoh-limits`. The record built from it equals the encoder's bytes."
      "Plan the Zenoh limits builder checks and the rows they hold to the record"
      {
        h.observedWhere "cases-observed" "zenoh_service_limits_builder_check" { h.count "casesObserved" 13; } "The checker counts ${CASES} honest checks. Four are the record's bytes, three ways and one reorder. Six hold the limits at the rows. Three are exact. One has a key that is not subscribed, one has two holders on one key, and one has a stack below the executable's. Three are of the record a spec derives. A builder that emits other bytes or refuses at a limit fails.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1af02-1d8b-7a48-9b9f-84747d5a4f72"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aecf-703a-b540-2c6d1cf6d094"
      "The exam refuses 15 manifests and 5 specs, and each refusal must come from the boundary that owns it. The refusal names its reason, and a refusal at another boundary fails the exam."
      "Plan the Zenoh limits builder checks and the rows they hold to the record"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_limits_builder_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 20; } "The checker refuses exactly ${CONTROLS} inputs: 15 manifests and 5 specs. Each is applied alone, and the honest input is accepted first. The refusal must name the reason of the boundary that owns it.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1af02-1d8b-7a48-9b9f-84747d5a4f72"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aecf-703a-b540-2c6e3059a9a7"
      "A composition with an instance named `zenoh-service` declares its limits. A spec without them is refused at admission."
      "Plan the Zenoh limits builder checks and the rows they hold to the record"
      {
        h.observedWhere "controls-refused" "zenoh_service_limits_builder_check" { h.count "negativeControlsRefused" 20; } "The checker refuses exactly ${CONTROLS} inputs: 15 manifests and 5 specs. Each is applied alone, and the honest input is accepted first. The refusal must name the reason of the boundary that owns it.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1af02-1d8b-7a48-9b9f-84747d5a4f72"; }; };
    (h.req "01a1b49c-aecf-703a-b540-2c6fb80479b3"
      "`just zenoh_service_limits_builder_check` exits zero and reports its observations through the gate adapter. It fails on `main` until the implementation lands."
      "Plan the Zenoh limits builder checks and the rows they hold to the record"
      {
        h.observedWhere "recipe-passed" "zenoh_service_limits_builder_check" h.noPredicates "The gate adapter reports the recipe's exit code, so the checker cannot vouch for itself. The recipe passes only after the implementation pull request merges, because the full run reads the builder it names.";
      }) with { supersedes = { "01a1af02-1d8b-7a48-9b9f-84747d5a4f72"; }; };
  }) with {
    nonGoals = {
      "rmw_zenoh peer interoperability, liveliness tokens, queryables, routers, gossip, multicast scouting and transport security: R1 and later own them.";
      "A physical Raspberry Pi 5 claim. Every observation here is a host or AArch64 QEMU observation.";
      "Editing R0 or any other pre-cutoff item. R0 is closed by hand on recorded evidence once this epic's acceptance holds.";
      "The ROSIDL importer and RIHS01 type-hash generator: the demo contract's checker derives those values today and this epic consumes them as frozen constants.";
      "Session state, timers, sequence-number management and the TCP link: the session slice owns them.";
      "Encoding any message the decoder refuses.";
      "Opening a socket, waiting on a Notification or reading a clock capability: the transport runtime slice owns them.";
      "Reconnection or resumption across a link loss; a new link is a new session under a fresh identity.";
      "A general ROSIDL importer, strings, sequences, nested types, CDR2 or big-endian output: the admitted message has two fixed-width fields.";
      "The RIHS01 type-hash and key-expression derivation, which the demo contract's checker owns today.";
      "Qualifying the network service's loopback stack, which has its own gates.";
      "Any ROS node API, executor or logging: the node slice owns them.";
      "An async runtime or a general heap: the profile's blocking, fixed-buffer shape is chosen to need neither.";
      "A general ROS 2 node API, executor, parameters or graph introspection; the nodes provide the demo's publish and receive behaviour and its log lines.";
      "Any grant to a router, gossip, multicast, discovery, DNS or a filesystem.";
      "Observing the loopback stack's own wire. The exchange crosses the service's loopback backend, so there is no packet capture; this observes the node codecs and session at the service's application boundary.";
      "Interoperability with an external rmw_zenoh peer, which R1 owns.";
      "Running the harness in CI. It needs the upstream crates from a registry, so the recipe is explicit and is not part of any aggregate.";
      "rmw_zenoh interoperability, a live Zenoh peer, or any packet capture. The harness compares codec and session behaviour in process.";
      "Changing the Profile 0 codec or session. A disagreement the harness finds is fixed by a separate change.";
      "Adding the zenoh crates to the root Cargo.lock, the closures, or the product build.";
      "rmw_zenoh interoperability, liveliness tokens, queryables, requests, a router or client peer, scouting or gossip, wildcard key expressions, best-effort frames, fragmentation and transport security. The 1.0.0 Python binding has no liveliness API, so no liveliness token was ever captured and none is claimed.";
      "Running a stock peer in CI. The capture is replayed from bytes; the live peer needs the eclipse-zenoh wheel from a registry and is an explicit, local experiment.";
      "A stock peer in the guest, a NIC, an external listener or a host-reachable port. This item is the Profile 0 session and link; reaching it from outside QEMU is a later item.";
      "Changing the existing Profile 0 refusals the first release still owns: 101 of the 102 refused vectors in vectors.txt keep their name, class and bytes, and the other one, transport_keep_alive, the single byte 0x04 that the stock peer sent four times, the checker names and lets be removed or stay refused. It may not become an accepted row: every accepted row is read by consumers that cannot be taught the stock syntax in the implementation PR (the encoder gate rebuilds each from its summary, the cross-check harness encodes each, and a Rust test counts them). No other refused vector may become accepted: the existing vectors with related names (an extension flag, an alias, a scope, a suffix, an OAM) were compared byte for byte with the capture and none matches, because the stock peer attaches a QoS extension and a body they lack. No accepted row may be added for a stock batch; the stock tests exercise them. Positions no captured stock batch used, such as an extension on a frame header, a subscriber declaration or a Put header, or an undeclare, stay refused.";
      "Peer discovery or scouting: peers stay statically wired, and the guest's authority still refuses a scouting request. A router or client peer, rmw_zenoh interoperability, liveliness tokens, queryables and requests.";
      "The optional attachment: a Put without the 33-byte rmw_zenoh attachment is still refused, in every configuration.";
      "Unreliable (best-effort) fragments, extensions on a fragment, interleaved fragmented messages, and a message above the heap a configuration declares: each is refused by name, and none is made to work.";
      "Running a stock peer in CI. The fragments are replayed from bytes; the live peer needs the eclipse-zenoh wheel from a registry and is an explicit local experiment.";
      "Raising the demo's bounds: the demo configuration, its twelve-byte payload and its one key and one subscriber are unchanged, and the 100 refused vectors the stock-peer exam pins keep their name, class and bytes. A heap in components/lib itself: the library takes storage from the component and gains no alloc dependency.";
      "A guest-to-host or host-to-guest exchange. Booting a composition with a NIC is a later item; this one is judged on the host.";
      "The bare form without the QoS extension. A stock peer's encoder would send it when it carries no QoS, but the pinned vector usub_missing_wire_expr_ext refuses it and the stock-peer item holds that vector; the capture this item rests on has the QoS. Profile 0 keeps refusing it, and that is a declared limit.";
      "Matching an undeclaration to a key. The form carries none; the session matches by id alone, as the upstream router does.";
      "An undeclaration of a subscriber the peer declared through an alias in a later frame, a second subscriber, and any peer but one eclipse-zenoh 1.0.0.";
      "Any change to the external-listener item's composition, guest or listener. That item is replaced by a successor that admits the bare form in its capture judge.";
      "Any product change in this item's planning PR: no decoder, session or Rust test module. They are the implementation's.";
      "Declaring more than one subscription through a link configuration. That needs a new version of `zenoh-link-limits/v1` and re-admits the links item.";
      "Telling the owner which subscription matched a sample. The service core item adds that.";
      "Wildcard keys, and subscriptions to a key that the peer has not declared.";
      "Any change to what the peer may declare. `per_side` keeps its meaning.";
      "Any product change in the planning PR. The session and the Rust test module belong to the implementation.";
      "How the grants reach the service at run time. That is a list in the system spec, a generation resource kind, a root-served read and a decoder in the service. The component item owns it.";
      "The service core, the client interface and any Zenoh behaviour. The core item judges those against a record of this contract.";
      "Wildcard keys, key aliases, and a holder that names a topic and a type for the service to turn into a key. A grant is one exact full key.";
      "Any product change in the planning PR. The generated Rust file and the system-spec grammar belong to the implementation.";
      "The component that wraps the core, the client interface, the path of the grants from the system spec to the service, and a booted composition. A later item owns them, and it cannot be graded until this one lands.";
      "A holder that names a topic and a type. Lazy declaration on the first subscribe. Reliable delivery with credits. A per-row option to exclude a holder's own publications. The decision record lists each as not taken.";
      "More than one peer, discovery, queryables, wildcard keys, and anything that the Profile 0 decoder refuses today.";
      "Any product change in the planning PR. The core, the event change and the Rust test module belong to the implementation.";
      "The client protocol and the client library in `components/lib`. The path of the grants from the system spec to the service. The component and a booted composition. Later items own them.";
      "Removing or changing the session-based core and its exam. They stay as merged.";
      "An acknowledgement from the peer. Profile 0 has none, so the core can know that the link took the bytes and no more.";
      "A bound on the notice queue other than the one the exam observes. The exam observes eight notices and records what a burst does to them.";
      "Any product change in the planning PR. The Rust modules and the link change belong to the implementation.";
      "Generated encoders and decoders for the layouts. The schema has no `gen_rust.zt`, which is product code. A later planning step owns the wire records and their bindings.";
      "The client library, the grants path, the service component and a booted composition. Later items own them.";
      "A holder with a sample larger than 4080 bytes. The grants contract allows larger samples and this version does not serve them.";
      "A request that names a key, a topic or a type.";
      "Any product change in the planning PR.";
      "Publishing the frames, which the LiDAR publisher item owns.";
      "Compressed MCAP chunks, other message types or more than one channel per store.";
      "Storing the frames in the guest filesystem or on a block device.";
      "The client adapter, the grants path, the service component and a booted composition. Other items own them.";
      "A change to `contracts/zenoh-service-client/v1`. The schema is landed and its item is done. This item reads it.";
      "A validator for the semantics of a record, such as which operation may carry which flag. The adapter owns it.";
      "A `gen_rust.zt` renderer. It is product code, and a planning PR cannot carry it. The generator is a script, as the grants and the client constants are.";
      "The service component, the grants path and a booted composition. Other items own them, and no service exists to attach to.";
      "Notifications, deadlines and timers. The adapter polls a bounded number of times, and a completion that does not arrive is lost.";
      "A sample larger than 4080 bytes. The protocol does not carry one.";
      "More than one outstanding request. The ring holds four slots and the adapter uses one.";
      "A change to the adapter's behavior. The behavior landed in the adapter item, and this item grades it.";
      "The real service. The test plays the service with a scripted stand-in, so what the real service does with an abort is not graded.";
      "An attach that has received only one loan. The adapter sends no abort there, and the item does not claim that this is right.";
      "A change to `contracts/zenoh-service-client/v1`.";
      "The read label, the manifest and system spec fields, the `slime-root` reader and the runtime wrapper. They change existing schemas and product code, so a planning PR cannot carry them. A later item owns them.";
      "The builder's use of the encoder. The encoder takes a list of rows, and this item does not wire it to a manifest field.";
      "The Zenoh service component and a booted composition.";
      "A change to `contracts/zenoh-service-grants/v1`. The record is landed. This item reads its alphabets.";
      "A row holder identity or a hash. The root serves the whole table to one named instance, so a row needs only the holder's name.";
      "Isolating two decoder guards. The row-count bound is reachable only by a buffer of 11 megabytes, and the total-length check refuses a header that claims more rows. The key-length guard is covered by the empty-segment check, because an empty key splits into one empty segment. Removing either guard changes no verdict the judge can show. Both stay in the decoder and are recorded as known limits.";
      "A system spec or a composition that declares grants. No composition has a `zenoh-service` instance, and the schema does not declare the two keys, so a `.zti` spec cannot carry them yet. A later item owns the schema fields.";
      "The read label, the manifest and system spec schema fields, the `slime-root` reader and the runtime wrapper. They change existing schemas and product code.";
      "A check that each holder has an endpoint to the service. The endpoint grants do not exist until the component does, so a later item owns it.";
      "A change to the `4096` object size the spec writes. Nothing checks it against a payload, and the table's size is its payload length.";
      "Adding the encoder and the table schema to the release inputs in `scripts/generate/generate-system-image-closures.py`. The builder runs `scripts/lib/zenoh_grants_table.py` and reads the table schema, and neither is a release input. The same holds for the entropy and network encoders in `scripts/build/generation_resources.py` and for `boot_contracts.py`. No composition declares grants, so no image can differ yet. A later item that enables a composition owns the release inputs for all of them.";
      "A change to the 363 tests that `just test_sel4_root` pins. CI runs that recipe, so raising the count before the tests exist would fail every pull request.";
      "Writing a data volume from a guest, or more than one payload on a disk.";
      "Reading the 99 MB LiDAR store in one finite plane. Such a plane's root serves 131072 requests before it stops, and a 4 KiB read costs about six, so about 80 MiB is the most one boot reads; the publisher item must lift that bound.";
      "Changing the object store or filesystem formats, or their 32 KiB object bound.";
      "Committing large data or fetching it from the network.";
      "A check that the two tests exercise the reader. The exam reads their names and counts from the run. Two empty tests with those names would pass. The implementation pull request is reviewed for that, and a checker-owned fixture would close it.";
      "The implementation. It is a separate pull request that carries every product change together, because `slime-root` cannot compile before the label exists in `slime-proto`.";
      "The documentation row for label 75 and the pin of 365. `check-syscall-abi` fails when the document and the contract disagree, and `just test_sel4_root` fails when the pin and the count disagree. Both land with the implementation.";
      "The ceiling entry in `scripts/lib/system_spec.py`. It reads a generated constant that does not exist until the schema declares it.";
      "A run of the reader through a booted root. No component reads the table, and the exam grades the reader by its host tests.";
      "A compile of the runtime wrapper. `just test_host` does not build that crate, so the exam reads the wrapper as text. The entropy wrapper is graded the same way.";
      "The Zenoh service component, its endpoint grants and a booted composition.";
      "Adding the encoder and the table schema to the release inputs. The decision record names this limit and a later item that enables a composition owns it.";
      "A third test. The exam requires exactly two. A test added later raises the count here and the pin in the same pull request.";
      "A check that the implementation's test drives the server. The test prints the transcript, and the judge reads what it prints. A test that printed the 39 expected lines without calling the server would pass. The implementation pull request is reviewed for that, and a checker-owned harness would close it.";
      "The server half. It is a module in `components/lib` that the implementation pull request adds with the component and the reader.";
      "The IO0 ring and the loans. The component owns them. The server half takes request bytes and returns completion bytes and the data page.";
      "The clock. The server half takes the time as an argument, and the exam advances it by one for each publication.";
      "What the component does when a holder faults or never detaches. The exam grades detach and abort as the protocol states them.";
      "A holder with more than two rows or a ring with more than two slots. The exam uses two holders with rows, one holder without, and a ring of two samples.";
      "The crate. The implementation pull request adds it with the server half and the grants reader.";
      "The holders' endpoints, the composition and the booted run. The composition item owns them.";
      "The stack size and the memory of the core and the link at real sizes. Nobody has computed them. The implementation states them in the component spec, and the exam does not check the values.";
      "The component's reaction to a holder that faults. The exam shows that the crate exists and does not show what its loop does.";
      "The composition and the generated outputs. The implementation pull request adds them.";
      "A boot of the arm. No image exists for it, and the marker chains have never matched a real transcript. The implementation pull request is the first to boot it and may need to tune the chains in a separate planning change.";
      "The choice of holders. The exam requires the service instance, the grants object and the arm's markers. It does not name the holders.";
      "A stock peer or an external network. The composition uses the network service's loopback backend.";
      "A CI job for the booted run. The owner decides that after the run has a measured duration.";
      "The closure sources. The implementation pull request adds the two closure inputs and regenerates every closure source in a derived commit, because it changes the closure input set.";
      "A publish-rate target. The elapsed time and late frames are recorded, not judged; reaching 10 Hz full-size is a separate performance item.";
      "A publish period or pass count chosen by the composition.";
      "rmw_zenoh graph discovery, liveliness tokens or QoS negotiation; the host side subscribes the data key directly.";
      "Raising the arrival ceiling of any existing composition.";
      "Physical hardware, including Raspberry Pi 5.";
